  "Model variance swaps at 30 days (k in [-3, 2], wings beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 extrapolated, so each inherits its model's wing bias): SVI-cal 16.79, SVI 16.87, eSSVI 16.18.",
  "Gap attribution (VIX, SVI-cal surface): replicated - official = +0.28. Strikes beyond the stored strip would add +0.01 under the surface's wing; the stored quotes beyond the fitted K/F 0.70-1.30 are 0.22 index points richer than that wing, so the truncation figure likely understates. Inside the fitted range market and surface differ by +0.10 (these two terms set the replication against the surface; they are not part of the gap). Left unexplained by the chain: -0.29 (official - replicated - truncation; 105% of official - replicated): snapshot timing vs the 16:15 ET print, stale quotes, rate."
